 in the rat</article-title>. <source>Eur. J. Neurosci.</source><volume>6</volume>, <fpage>429</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>453</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1460-9568.1994.tb00286.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8019680</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2006</year>). <article-title>Parallel thalamic pathways for whisking and touch signals in the rat</article-title>. <source>PLoS Biol.</source><volume>4</volume>, <fpage>e124</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pbio.0040124</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16605304</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2006</year>). <article-title>Central sensitization in thalamic nociceptive neurons induced by mustard oil application to rat molar tooth pulp</article-title>. <source>Neuroscience</source><volume>142</volume>, <fpage>833</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>842</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neuroscience.2006.06.063</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16934945</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>